From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qdsp6: q6core: only an unsupported GET_STATE means "assume up"

__q6core_is_adsp_ready() cleared get_state_supported before each
AVCS_CMD_ADSP_EVENT_GET_STATE query, and only a real
AVCS_CMDRSP_ADSP_EVENT_GET_STATE response set it again. So a timeout,
or a basic response with any error status, fell through to "assume
the DSP is up": the check answered "ready" exactly when the DSP was
too early to answer. Only an explicit ADSP_EUNSUPPORTED means the
query does not exist; anything else is now "not ready", and the
caller polls again.

q6core_is_adsp_ready() also polled with no delay, so a DSP that
answers at once would be flooded with queries for up to 3 s while it
comes up. Sleep 50 ms between queries, as the downstream audio stack
does.

Nothing calls q6core_is_adsp_ready() yet; the next patch makes q6afe
wait on it.

[ARMDeck: from Nova-Deck os-build, kernel/patches/0893 (commit 325dfde9a380),
unchanged; it applies to 6.16.7 as is. Needed by 0013, which is the first
caller of q6core_is_adsp_ready().]

---
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6core.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6core.c
index 49cfb32..48fa8fd 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6core.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6core.c
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 // Copyright (c) 2011-2017, The Linux Foundation. All rights reserved.
 // Copyright (c) 2018, Linaro Limited
 
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 #include <linux/wait.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
@@ -15,6 +16,7 @@
 #include "q6dsp-errno.h"
 
 #define ADSP_STATE_READY_TIMEOUT_MS    3000
+#define ADSP_STATE_POLL_MS             50
 #define Q6_READY_TIMEOUT_MS 100
 #define AVCS_CMD_ADSP_EVENT_GET_STATE		0x0001290C
 #define AVCS_CMDRSP_ADSP_EVENT_GET_STATE	0x0001290D
@@ -209,7 +211,15 @@ static bool __q6core_is_adsp_ready(struct q6core *core)
 	struct apr_pkt pkt;
 	int rc;
 
-	core->get_state_supported = false;
+	/*
+	 * Only an explicit ADSP_EUNSUPPORTED means the query does not exist
+	 * and the DSP should be assumed up. No answer, or any other error,
+	 * is a DSP that is not ready yet: report it so, and let the caller
+	 * poll again.
+	 */
+	core->get_state_supported = true;
+	core->avcs_state = 0;
+	core->resp_received = false;
 
 	pkt.hdr.hdr_field = APR_HDR_FIELD(APR_MSG_TYPE_SEQ_CMD,
 				      APR_HDR_LEN(APR_HDR_SIZE), APR_PKT_VER);
@@ -318,6 +328,9 @@ bool q6core_is_adsp_ready(void)
 			ret = false;
 			break;
 		}
+
+		/* A DSP still coming up answers at once; don't flood it. */
+		msleep(ADSP_STATE_POLL_MS);
 	}
 
 	mutex_unlock(&g_core->lock);
